## 4. Source patcher safety behaviour

Before writing, the patcher:

1. Reads all five target files.
2. Verifies each exact source fragment and expected occurrence count.
3. Builds all patched content in memory.
4. Confirms that none of the five `.pre-universal-risk-v1.bak` files already exists.
5. Creates all five backups before changing any source file.
6. Writes source files atomically. If a write fails, it attempts to restore every original source file from the in-memory originals and leaves the backup files available for inspection.

A source mismatch, missing file, unexpected line-count category or existing backup causes an abort. Do not delete or overwrite an existing backup to force a rerun; inspect the repository state first.

